it you know turn  based it's a little bit more freestyle  than your traditional turn base but I do  think that this is a good middle ground  I would prefer The Bravery default in  the Final Fantasy Tactics gameplay but  this was a good second place going to  that there's scale trees to pretty much  anything you could think of they  actually have individual unit skill  trees that it is a little bit less  in-depth in the actual skill tray on the  weapons but I do think it's a nice  little touch to give people a little bit  more incentive to actually grind out  those sections you get those SP points  for actually leveling up your character  and then you get skill tree points and  those are known as SP now let me explain  to you a little bit on the dial Phil  Chronicle and how they like to do stuff  in this game the SP is something that  you get for Unique uh circumstances that  you get during the mission it's kind of  like bonus content that you get for  doing the mission in a certain way the  majority of the time if not every bonus  content that you get on missions is to  either a keep everyone alive never have  anyone fall or B do it in a certain time  limit now for the most part you want to  generally do both you don't want anyone  dying and you don't want anyone to take  so long that you don't get that bone  bonus time limit that you also get now  you'll get the material to make weapons  and you'll also get the skill points  required to level up the actual skills  that are required for that weapon now  everyone has different things now it's  not like one of the class systems I do  prefer the class system I will come out  there openly on that I don't mind this  system I think it was done fairly well  in terms of you know balancing out your  actual individual skill points with the  weapon skills and building the weapon I  think it worked out pretty well and I  think this is a decent system but I  still prefer the job system because I  want to be able to pick and modify who I  want and to do what I want them to do I  want to be able to build a warrior that  has some form of skills related to like  a Time Mage where you can have Auto  haste on now none of that was present in  this game and I don't think that I'm  going to really dock them for not doing  something another game does but I do  feel like what they did here is a solid  foundation and I have to respect them  for because the game is fun one thing I  can really enjoy what they've done with  this combat is they've actually given  you the ability to replay old missions  to level up and what I mean level up is  you can go with these bonus requirements  on these older missions let's say you  messed them up because the crazy part  about this game is those skill points  let's say you never do it in a certain  time limit or people are always dying  you're never getting these skill points  unless you level up the actual entirety  of your clan to get a huge sizable ones  every time you level up so that's the  only time you're going to be leveling  them up so this game actually is very  hard and if you don't play the game the  game wants you to play it so if you  don't do these things and I don't think  they do a good job explaining how you  get these SP or at least additional XPS  if you do these certain missions in a  certain way and they could have did a  little bit better on that I also feel  like they are certain you know life  change qualities that they should have  done here now let me explain to you how  the actual system unit system is set up  so you got primary units and you got  secondary units the cool thing about is  you can mix and match the primary and  secondary pretty much the primary is  going to be the person that's on the  field at all times and you want that  secondary to complement that primary  unit so if you got it like a flying unit  you want that secondary unit to  complement the attacks that primary unit  can do so let's say that you have a unit  that do